---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Experience from '../components/Experience.astro';
import { industries, hqLine, ownershipStatement, ownershipPhrase } from '../config';

const description = `Direwolf Cybersecurity is ${ownershipPhrase} headquartered in Colorado Springs, Colorado, built to bring enterprise-grade security operations to small and mid-size organizations and government contractors.`;
const lede = `Direwolf Cybersecurity is ${ownershipPhrase} headquartered in Colorado Springs, Colorado. We built the Direwolf Platform so that small and mid-size organizations can have the kind of security operations that large enterprises take for granted.`;
---

<BaseLayout title="About us" description={description}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About us"
    title="Serious security for organizations that are not large enterprises"
    lede={lede}
  />

  <Section id="mission" eyebrow="Our mission" title="Protection that does not depend on size">
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p>
        Most organizations that handle sensitive work are small. They have a handful of IT staff at
        best, no security team, and the same adversaries as everyone else. Frameworks such as NIST
        SP 800-171 ask them to monitor, respond, and keep evidence, on the budget of a small
        business.
      </p>
      <p>
        We started Direwolf to close that gap. By running security operations with AI, with a human
        analyst reviewing its decisions, and by automating everything from purchase to deployment,
        we can offer monitoring and response at a price a small organization can carry, without
        cutting corners on the parts that matter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="who-we-are"
    tone="surface"
    eyebrow="Who we are"
    title="Cyber professionals from regulated industries"
  >
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p>
        Our team&rsquo;s experience comes from inside regulated and high-stakes environments. We
        have worked in:
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {industries.map((industry) => (
        <li class="card py-4 text-sm font-medium">{industry}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <p>
        That background shapes how we work. We document what we do, we assume an assessor will read
        it, and we tell customers plainly what is in place and what is not.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="government-contractors"
    eyebrow="Government contracting"
    title="A specialty in organizations held to a higher standard"
  >
    <div class="prose mt-6">
      <p>
        Our specialty is government contractors and subcontractors that must meet high compliance
        standards: organizations with safeguarding requirements under DFARS and the Cybersecurity
        Maturity Model Certification (CMMC) program. We understand what NIST SP 800-171 asks for, we
        designed the Direwolf Platform around those requirements, and we are documenting the shared
        responsibilities so that your system security plan and your assessment line up.
      </p>
      <p>
        Direwolf itself is aligned to NIST SP 800-171 and pursuing CMMC Level 2 certification. See
        our <a href="/compliance/">Compliance</a> page for the current status and exactly what we do
        and do not claim.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="company"
    tone="surface"
    eyebrow="Company"
    title="Service-disabled veteran-owned, Colorado-based"
  >
    <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card">
        <dt class="font-semibold">Headquarters</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted mt-2 text-sm">{hqLine}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <dt class="font-semibold">Ownership</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted mt-2 text-sm">
          {ownershipStatement}. Certified by the U.S. Small Business Administration through its
          Veteran Small Business Certification (VetCert) program.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <dt class="font-semibold">Hosting</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted mt-2 text-sm">
          Where the Direwolf Platform runs, and what that does and does not mean for your compliance
          program, is explained on our
          <a href="/compliance/" class="link">
            Compliance
          </a>{' '}
          page.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <dt class="font-semibold">Equal opportunity employer</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted mt-2 text-sm">
          Direwolf Cybersecurity is an equal opportunity employer. We make employment decisions
          without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity,
          national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by
          law. Read our{' '}
          <a href="/legal/eeo/" class="link">
            EEO statement
          </a>
          .
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </Section>

  <Experience variant="full" />

  <CallToAction
    title="Want to talk to us?"
    text="We are glad to discuss your environment, your compliance obligations, and whether Direwolf is the right fit."
  />
</BaseLayout>
